      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Key Concepts on the go \n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Key Concepts on the go \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Y3jegDnt_wNByJWdgpEyA",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1535.2716770822356,
      "y": 72.28023859991941,
      "width": 824.6423705826081,
      "height": 1025,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0j",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 526339248,
      "version": 8622,
      "versionNonce": 944360832,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1765420054670,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1) For problems where we are making a get request for multiple rows of data like\nproblem list, leaderboard etc etc we can and must use pagination. \n2) Sql vs NoSql: While both will work fine, for this problem we are not executing\ncomplex SQL queries so we can go ahead with noSql. \n3) We use a Monaco Editor to allow user to code their solution in the browser. \n4) Solution Submission: Now this is the crux of this problem. \n    - Bad Solution: run code on the same server\n    Issues: security, Performance, Isolation\n    - Good Solution: create a VM and run in it \n    Issues: VM is resource intensive, time consuming setting up vm\n    - Great Sol A: Using docker container for each runtime that we support (e.g.\nPython, JavaScript, Java) that installs the necessary dependencies and runs the\ncode in a sandboxed environment.\n    Challenges: configure and secure the containers to prevent users from breaking\nout of the container and accessing the host system. We also need to enforce\nresource limits to prevent any single submission from utilizing excessive system\nresources and affecting other users.\n    - Great Sol B: Serverless functions \n5) View LeaderBoard: \n    - Simple Solution(Polling with db queries): query submission table based on\ncompetition id, group by userId, order by number of successful submissions\n        Issues: High database load and not sustainable with time. \n    - Good Solution(Caching with periodic update): Introduce a cache and update it\nevery 30 sec with some chron job\n        Issue: polling still there and not realtime actually. \n    - Great Solution(Using a cache with sorted set): When a submission is\nprocessed, both the database and the Redis sorted set are updated. Clients poll\nthe server every 5 seconds for leaderboard updates, and the server returns the\ntop N users from the Redis sorted set which is wicked fast and requires no\nexpensive database queries. \n\n6) Running test cases: \nLanguage-agnostic test execution is achieved by defining test cases once in a\nstandard format (JSON with serialized inputs/outputs) and implementing language-\nspecific deserializers that convert serialized data into native objects before\npassing them to user code, comparing outputs against expected results.\n\nEach language gets a lightweight test harness that handles deserialization logic,\neliminating the need to maintain separate test suites while supporting any\nprogramming language.\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1) For problems where we are making a get request for multiple rows of data like problem list, leaderboard etc etc we can and must use pagination. \n2) Sql vs NoSql: While both will work fine, for this problem we are not executing complex SQL queries so we can go ahead with noSql. \n3) We use a Monaco Editor to allow user to code their solution in the browser. \n4) Solution Submission: Now this is the crux of this problem. \n    - Bad Solution: run code on the same server\n    Issues: security, Performance, Isolation\n    - Good Solution: create a VM and run in it \n    Issues: VM is resource intensive, time consuming setting up vm\n    - Great Sol A: Using docker container for each runtime that we support (e.g. Python, JavaScript, Java) that installs the necessary dependencies and runs the code in a sandboxed environment.\n    Challenges: configure and secure the containers to prevent users from breaking out of the container and accessing the host system. We also need to enforce resource limits to prevent any single submission from utilizing excessive system resources and affecting other users.\n    - Great Sol B: Serverless functions \n5) View LeaderBoard: \n    - Simple Solution(Polling with db queries): query submission table based on competition id, group by userId, order by number of successful submissions\n        Issues: High database load and not sustainable with time. \n    - Good Solution(Caching with periodic update): Introduce a cache and update it every 30 sec with some chron job\n        Issue: polling still there and not realtime actually. \n    - Great Solution(Using a cache with sorted set): When a submission is processed, both the database and the Redis sorted set are updated. Clients poll the server every 5 seconds for leaderboard updates, and the server returns the top N users from the Redis sorted set which is wicked fast and requires no expensive database queries. \n\n6) Running test cases: \nLanguage-agnostic test execution is achieved by defining test cases once in a standard format (JSON with serialized inputs/outputs) and implementing language-specific deserializers that convert serialized data into native objects before passing them to user code, comparing outputs against expected results.\n\nEach language gets a lightweight test harness that handles deserialization logic, eliminating the need to maintain separate test suites while supporting any programming language.\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
